          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Introduction"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Graphs are used every day to represent real-world situations: tracking a journey on a distance-time graph, converting between currencies, monitoring temperature changes, or comparing costs. Being able to read, draw, and interpret these graphs is one of the most practical mathematical skills you will learn."
          }
        ]
      },
